{"type":"message","id":"f58607b7","parentId":"5c07be8e","timestamp":"2026-05-11T07:16:44.186Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_RZzTgZKGAyrytu6slfzew0iQ|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a01825bfc088191bb66d19c9a173482","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Dashboard MVP\n\nLocal, static, read-only dashboard concept for Albert and neodaemon.\n\nSecurity principles:\n- Local files only for now.\n- No public exposure.\n- No network service started automatically.\n- No credentials or secrets stored here.\n- MVP first, iterate slowly.\n\nInitial blocks:\n1. Today\n2. Health / mobility\n3. Habits\n4. Pending / chaos inbox\n5. LLM token usage snapshot\n6. Token efficiency: “tokens per useful task”\n7. System health / stability score\n8. Tools / plugins audit\n\nToken efficiency MVP:\n- Source: `/openclaw/workspace/metrics/token_efficiency/YYYY/MM/DD.jsonl`\n- Current values are estimated from `session_status` snapshots, not exact per-task accounting.\n- Channels are grouped as Telegram, TUI, automations, subagents, or unknown.\n- Visual bars are static CSS, with no external libraries or network calls.\n\nStability MVP:\n- Source: `/openclaw/workspace/metrics/stability/YYYY/MM/DD.json`\n- Phase 1 is observe-only: no automatic gateway restarts, no tool freezing, no external alerts.\n- Shows uptime, RAM, CPU load, approximate tokens/hour, critical errors, loops, confirmed gateway restarts, anomalous consumption, and a daily stability score.\n\nTools/plugins audit MVP:\n- Source: `/openclaw/workspace/metrics/tools_plugins/YYYY/MM/DD.json`\n- Read-only inventory: plugins discovered/loaded/disabled, plugin doctor status, eligible skills, active automations, and prudential warnings.\n- No plugin/tool is disabled from the dashboard; changes require explicit Albert approval.\n\nQuick launcher:\n- Script: `/openclaw/workspace/dashboard/open-dashboard.sh`\n- Desktop entry: `/openclaw/workspace/dashboard/neodaemon-dashboard.desktop`\n- The launcher starts a local-only server on `127.0.0.1:8765` and opens the dashboard in the browser.\n\nOpen `index.html` locally when explicitly approved/needed.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778483804186}}
{"type":"message","id":"bf8dd70f","parentId":"f58607b7","timestamp":"2026-05-11T07:17:40.718Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Editing HTML with Python**\n\nI'm thinking about editing HTML and using a Python script to make it easier. It could help streamline the process, especially if I need to test certain sections. I also want to ensure that I can insert styles and scripts effectively. I might have to find a way to preserve some elements while I do this. Overall, using Python seems like a smart approach for handling HTML adjustments.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a01825d08d48191a5d39a2a72ecaba5\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqAYJhygp-i6xihijUUjxJ0zcg-vSeQlfwMtmMd9Mz1QDvzCDq120wwkRMgS09SNVOT7BQouCfQfoS8iwff-6-wtn-lc15TAK79gsmhK5KqGyKNNvB6yDelCyCgAsCQOL-QNe7qkpCgo78W9MKeETjHDIq2VgPRstZxIsmlaaB3H-Wra6Gstat7Re7zHlh-OiUJ28pjd1bx5cOtPeYRy-FySVl9gS31tgiTyRX4Cv1acy_GOGzGTQZde6ZFmmAlCHcdMSzOAckmzgkZL-liAFO2AwIwM0YJX0b4__LhpcudxYi-xU5fje7e3w8mTeXVaW1OoXAltVsEALEsOQiWbmiSotQ31TuDwtFtZU1cFOLP_si_aB1EkkU_HuM8EaDMw7lYtUtUAIv7wQK2DvyFh_y7-J6JEw2K3UkKRkvjaOstHOWqZwD02nxE5EIuaiHU9nyP3Em7-iOrelVGRf3l0R_l0iyqvhVRlbEMjsm1g5eIKxINyUivfqiqc2ArH9or1jMkAf52LBvkXNEY7JmlnmHawzzlMrh92ppK6OsnMrJX8-KpuA23HruwET297d0ulKHub-oEDi18UelNGTtfffVzVBN1LVBF4qP13TXCD1jIerHpFW626F8tlmlLiHDub6M1xWRQ8LXEaXo-OkEn78iIM3N8ijqVFHY-V6TBvlNRAlhoymqt2r29H7HOkq5-u3UKMvLOAWKWULISkY-gZ_t2hI6A6nuEGuf6Ps4EPWTcGunHeN8-iX1SVdtCtMNRxMBrfgaeXDvIBcSv5gY1ueU50ecf7EQnJ4Hf1h53TjUnZAVBHpdtnsPe_J6fTTGmjKUvRsU15n-7bENa-9sO94zMtqAeEoWf20ZDT4RX3TWsXot_b409oCny_0JH7HeHYj4CCfywZO3RMt72S-2tm41YHJPuD3wT5qzuJ7--bCiP_QJUKfQPpJWDzrhMunwgM8rcW8pvO02vXGqF8etTrS4cjP7LHB33NUKpuP_0-lKk7h3djsO8H3tnUlbYpAqef10-qi9t7s8T5atVuTJNI6Sz5Gjild4BGJNKBs1Yt9cjl4q4mTdjA0uHyr54UqJVwq3Cyab\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Editing HTML with Python**\\n\\nI'm thinking about editing HTML and using a Python script to make it easier. It could help streamline the process, especially if I need to test certain sections. I also want to ensure that I can insert styles and scripts effectively. I might have to find a way to preserve some elements while I do this. Overall, using Python seems like a smart approach for handling HTML adjustments.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_JXOSxiIl8H1WQgnaoIobaroP|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a018261a17081919d14a1497a4e2337","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('/openclaw/workspace/dashboard/index.html')\ns=p.read_text()\nstyle_insert='''\\n    .wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }\\n    .form-row {\\n      display: grid;\\n      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(120px, 1fr));\\n      gap: 10px;\\n      margin-bottom: 12px;\\n    }\\n    label { color: var(--muted); font-size: .88rem; }\\n    input, button {\\n      width: 100%;\\n      margin-top: 4px;\\n      border-radius: 10px;\\n      border: 1px solid var(--border);\\n      background: var(--panel-2);\\n      color: var(--text);\\n      padding: 10px;\\n      font: inherit;\\n    }\\n    button {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      background: var(--accent);\\n      color: #07111f;\\n      border: 0;\\n      font-weight: 700;\\n    }\\n    button.secondary {\\n      background: var(--panel-2);\\n      color: var(--muted);\\n      border: 1px solid var(--border);\\n    }\\n    canvas {\\n      width: 100%;\\n      height: 220px;\\n      display: block;\\n      background: #0b1017;\\n      border: 1px solid var(--border);\\n      border-radius: 12px;\\n      margin: 8px 0 12px;\\n    }\\n    .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }\\n    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .92rem; }\\n    th, td { padding: 8px 6px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); text-align: left; }\\n    th { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }\\n    .actions { display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }\\n    .actions button { width: auto; min-width: 150px; }\\n'''\ns=s.replace('''    .small { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }\\n    footer {''','''    .small { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }'''+style_insert+'''\\n    footer {''')\nsection='''\\n      <section class=\"wide\" id=\"blood-pressure-section\">\\n        <h2>Tensión arterial</h2>\\n        <p class=\"small\">Registro privado en este navegador. Guarda sistólica, diastólica, pulso y la fecha/hora de introducción.</p>\\n        <form id=\"bp-form\">\\n          <div class=\"form-row\">\\n            <label>Sistólica\\n              <input id=\"bp-sys\" type=\"number\" inputmode=\"numeric\" min=\"60\" max=\"260\" placeholder=\"120\" required />\\n            </label>\\n            <label>Diastólica\\n              <input id=\"bp-dia\" type=\"number\" inputmode=\"numeric\" min=\"40\" max=\"160\" placeholder=\"80\" required />\\n            </label>\\n            <label>Pulso opcional\\n              <input id=\"bp-pulse\" type=\"number\" inputmode=\"numeric\" min=\"30\" max=\"220\" placeholder=\"70\" />\\n            </label>\\n            <label>Fecha y hora\\n              <input id=\"bp-datetime\" type=\"datetime-local\" required />\\n            </label>\\n          </div>\\n          <div class=\"actions\">\\n            <button type=\"submit\">Añadir lectura</button>\\n            <button class=\"secondary\" id=\"bp-export\" type=\"button\">Exportar JSON</button>\\n            <button class=\"secondary\" id=\"bp-clear\" type=\"button\">Borrar registros</button>\\n          </div>\\n        </form>\\n        <canvas id=\"bp-chart\" width=\"900\" height=\"260\" aria-label=\"Gráfica de tensión arterial\" role=\"img\"></canvas>\\n        <div class=\"table-wrap\">\\n          <table>\\n            <thead>\\n              <tr><th>Fecha</th><th>Sistólica</th><th>Diastólica</th><th>Pulso</th></tr>\\n            </thead>\\n            <tbody id=\"bp-table-body\">\\n              <tr><td colspan=\"4\" class=\"small\">Todavía no hay lecturas.</td></tr>\\n            </tbody>\\n          </table>\\n        </div>\\n        <span class=\"pill\">MVP local · datos en localStorage</span>\\n      </section>\\n'''\ns=s.replace('''      <section>\\n        <h2>Hábitos</h2>''', section+'''\\n      <section>\\n        <h2>Hábitos</h2>''')\nscript='''\\n  <script>\\n    const BP_STORAGE_KEY = 'neodaemon.dashboard.bloodPressure.v1';\\n\\n    function localDatetimeValue(date = new Date()) {\\n      const offsetMs = date.getTimezoneOffset() * 60000;\\n      return new Date(date.getTime() - offsetMs).toISOString().slice(0, 16);\\n    }\\n\\n    function loadBpReadings() {\\n      try {\\n        return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(BP_STORAGE_KEY) || '[]')\\n          .filter(r => Number.isFinite(r.systolic) && Number.isFinite(r.diastolic) && r.recordedAt)\\n          .sort((a, b) => new Date(a.recordedAt) - new Date(b.recordedAt));\\n      } catch {\\n        return [];\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    function saveBpReadings(readings) {\\n      localStorage.setItem(BP_STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(readings));\\n    }\\n\\n    function formatDate(value) {\\n      return new Intl.DateTimeFormat('es-ES', {\\n        dateStyle: 'short',\\n        timeStyle: 'short'\\n      }).format(new Date(value));\\n    }\\n\\n    function drawBpChart(readings) {\\n      const canvas = document.getElementById('bp-chart');\\n      const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\\n      const w = canvas.width;\\n      const h = canvas.height;\\n      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, w, h);\\n      ctx.fillStyle = '#0b1017';\\n      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, w, h);\\n\\n      const pad = { left: 48, right: 18, top: 20, bottom: 34 };\\n      const minY = 40;\\n      const maxY = 200;\\n      const xFor = i => readings.length === 1\\n        ? (pad.left + (w - pad.left - pad.right) / 2)\\n        : pad.left + i * ((w - pad.left - pad.right) / (readings.length - 1));\\n      const yFor = value => pad.top + (maxY - value) * ((h - pad.top - pad.bottom) / (maxY - minY));\\n\\n      ctx.strokeStyle = '#30363d';\\n      ctx.fillStyle = '#8b949e';\\n      ctx.font = '13px system-ui, sans-serif';\\n      [60, 80, 120, 140, 180].forEach(v => {\\n        const y = yFor(v);\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.moveTo(pad.left, y);\\n        ctx.lineTo(w - pad.right, y);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n        ctx.fillText(String(v), 8, y + 4);\\n      });\\n\\n      if (!readings.length) {\\n        ctx.fillStyle = '#8b949e';\\n        ctx.fillText('Añade tu primera lectura para ver la gráfica.', pad.left, h / 2);\\n        return;\\n      }\\n\\n      function plot(key, color, label) {\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = color;\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 3;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        readings.forEach((r, i) => {\\n          const x = xFor(i);\\n          const y = yFor(r[key]);\\n          if (i === 0) ctx.moveTo(x, y); else ctx.lineTo(x, y);\\n        });\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n        readings.forEach((r, i) => {\\n          ctx.fillStyle = color;\\n          ctx.beginPath();\\n          ctx.arc(xFor(i), yFor(r[key]), 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n          ctx.fill();\\n        });\\n        ctx.fillStyle = color;\\n        ctx.fillText(label, w - pad.right - 120, key === 'systolic' ? 22 : 42);\\n      }\\n\\n      plot('systolic', '#ff7b72', 'Sistólica');\\n      plot('diastolic', '#58a6ff', 'Diastólica');\\n\\n      ctx.fillStyle = '#8b949e';\\n      readings.forEach((r, i) => {\\n        if (i % Math.ceil(readings.length / 5) === 0 || i === readings.length - 1) {\\n          ctx.fillText(formatDate(r.recordedAt).replace(', ', '\\\\n'), Math.max(48, xFor(i) - 28), h - 10);\\n        }\\n      });\\n    }\\n\\n    function renderBp() {\\n      const readings = loadBpReadings();\\n      const body = document.getElementById('bp-table-body');\\n      if (!readings.length) {\\n        body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan=\"4\" class=\"small\">Todavía no hay lecturas.</td></tr>';\\n      } else {\\n        body.innerHTML = readings.slice().reverse().map(r => `\\n          <tr>\\n            <td>${formatDate(r.recordedAt)}</td>\\n            <td>${r.systolic}</td>\\n            <td>${r.diastolic}</td>\\n            <td>${r.pulse || '—'}</td>\\n          </tr>\\n        `).join('');\\n      }\\n      drawBpChart(readings);\\n    }\\n\\n    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\\n      document.getElementById('bp-datetime').value = localDatetimeValue();\\n      document.getElementById('bp-form').addEventListener('submit', event => {\\n        event.preventDefault();\\n        const reading = {\\n          systolic: Number(document.getElementById('bp-sys').value),\\n          diastolic: Number(document.getElementById('bp-dia').value),\\n          pulse: document.getElementById('bp-pulse').value ? Number(document.getElementById('bp-pulse').value) : null,\\n          recordedAt: new Date(document.getElementById('bp-datetime').value).toISOString(),\\n          createdAt: new Date().toISOString()\\n        };\\n        const readings = loadBpReadings();\\n        readings.push(reading);\\n        saveBpReadings(readings);\\n        event.target.reset();\\n        document.getElementById('bp-datetime').value = localDatetimeValue();\\n        renderBp();\\n      });\\n      document.getElementById('bp-export').addEventListener('click', () => {\\n        const blob = new Blob([JSON.stringify(loadBpReadings(), null, 2)], { type: 'application/json' });\\n        const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);\\n        const a = document.createElement('a');\\n        a.href = url;\\n        a.download = 'tension-arterial.json';\\n        a.click();\\n        URL.revokeObjectURL(url);\\n      });\\n      document.getElementById('bp-clear').addEventListener('click', () => {\\n        if (confirm('¿Borrar todos los registros de tensión arterial guardados en este navegador?')) {\\n          localStorage.removeItem(BP_STORAGE_KEY);\\n          renderBp();\\n        }\\n      });\\n      renderBp();\\n    });\\n  </script>\\n'''\ns=s.replace('</body>\\n</html>\\n', script+'</body>\\n</html>\\n')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom html.parser import HTMLParser\nfrom pathlib import Path\nHTMLParser().feed(Path('/openclaw/workspace/dashboard/index.html').read_text())\nprint('html parse ok')\nPY","workdir":"/openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":985,"output":3082,"cacheRead":18432,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22499,"cost":{"input":0.0049250000000000006,"output":0.09246,"cacheRead":0.009216,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.106601}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778483804188,"responseId":"resp_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a01825c741481918f5d59fe0a1bbee2"}}
