{"type":"message","id":"20fcf23d","parentId":"89e77445","timestamp":"2026-05-11T07:35:08.278Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_038xukGlukIfdOd18goEqnfx|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a0186a53e2881919f59d6e0b0a3a149","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"set -e\nbash -n dashboard/open-dashboard.sh\npython3 -m http.server 8766 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory /openclaw/workspace >/tmp/dashboard-test.log 2>&1 & pid=$!; sleep 1\ncurl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8766/dashboard/ | grep -q 'loadServerBpReadings'\ncurl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8766/health/blood_pressure/2026/05/11.jsonl | grep -q '\"systolic\":121'\nkill $pid; wait $pid 2>/dev/null || true\nprintf '%s\\n' '- Corrección importante: el lanzador del dashboard ahora sirve la raíz del workspace y abre `/dashboard/`, para que la gráfica pueda leer `/health/blood_pressure/YYYY/MM/DD.jsonl`. Así los valores dictados por Telegram no solo se guardan: también aparecen en la gráfica al recargar.' >> /openclaw/workspace/memory/2026/05/11.md\necho 'launcher and graph data path check ok'","workdir":"/openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":827,"output":277,"cacheRead":52736,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":53840,"cost":{"input":0.004135000000000001,"output":0.00831,"cacheRead":0.026368,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.038813}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778484897749,"responseId":"resp_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a0186a201c481919c0abef094b4777f"}}
