ext\",\"text\":\"**Considering skill creation**\\n\\nI'm thinking about creating a skill in OpenClaw. It seems like I should look into the workspace and available skills, but the user mentioned they want something new. I might need to explore local documentation for installation paths. Overall, it sounds like I need to search for more information about setting up and creating this new skill to ensure everything runs smoothly. Let's look into that!\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7U5zRndebMv6AF2Y6UUGeVMc|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a018ba69c688191866cf526248bb14f","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -R \"\\.openclaw.*skills\\|skills/.*SKILL.md\\|AgentSkills\" -n /usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs /usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills 2>/dev/null | head -100","workdir":"/openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":779,"output":139,"cacheRead":78336,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":79254,"cost":{"input":0.0038950000000000005,"output":0.00417,"cacheRead":0.039168,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.047233000000000004}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778486178647,"responseId":"resp_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a018ba2d51481919f38afe687238d47"}}
{"type":"message","id":"35f35523","parentId":"7618f316","timestamp":"2026-05-11T07:56:23.334Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7U5zRndebMv6AF2Y6UUGeVMc|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a018ba69c688191866cf526248bb14f","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/audit-checks.md:99:| `skills.workspace.symlink_escape`                             | warn          | Workspace `skills/**/SKILL.md` resolves outside workspace root (symlink-chain drift) | workspace `skills/**` filesystem state                                                               | no       |\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-examples.md:480:      { id: \"docs\", workspace: \"~/.openclaw/workspace-docs\", skills: [\"docs-search\"] },\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/plugins/voice-call.md:712:This repo ships a matching skill doc at `skills/voice-call/SKILL.md`.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/plugins/skill-workshop.md:21:<workspace>/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/setup.md:35:- **Workspace:** `~/.openclaw/workspace` (skills, prompts, memories; make it a private git repo)\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/install/docker-vm-runtime.md:129:| Skill configs       | `/home/node/.openclaw/skills/`                         | Host volume mount      | Skill-level state                                             |\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/clawhub.md:133:If you already use `~/.openclaw/skills` or bundled skills, workspace\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/clawhub.md:437:    `~/openclaw/skills` and `~/.openclaw/skills`). This is designed to\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/creating-skills.md:21:    mkdir -p ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/hello-world\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/creating-skills.md:111:| `~/.openclaw/skills/`           | Medium     | Shared (all agents)   |\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/skills-config.md:85:- Built-in skill roots always include `~/.openclaw/skills`, `~/.agents/skills`,\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/skills-config.md:117:  `~/.agents/skills` → `~/.openclaw/skills` → bundled skills →\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/skills.md:11:OpenClaw uses **[AgentSkills](https://agentskills.io)-compatible** skill\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/skills.md:26:| 4   | Managed/local skills  | `~/.openclaw/skills`             |\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/skills.md:49:| Shared managed/local | `~/.openclaw/skills`                        | All agents on that machine  |\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/skills.md:142:`skills/<group>/<skill>/SKILL.md`, so related third-party skills can be\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/skills.md:177:OpenClaw follows the AgentSkills spec for layout/intent. The parser used\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/skills.md:262:`metadata.openclaw` is absent, so older installed skills keep their\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/skills.md:271:- Example: the `summarize` skill (`skills/summarize/SKILL.md`) needs the `summarize` CLI in the sandbox container to run there.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/skills.md:366:defines `metadata.openclaw.skillKey`, use that key under `skills.entries`.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/skills.md:466:install (npm package or OpenClaw.app). `~/.openclaw/skills` exists for\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:111:- `~/.openclaw/agents/<agentId>/agent/codex-home/` (per-agent Codex runtime account, config, skills, plugins, and native thread state)\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent-workspace.md:114:- `~/.openclaw/skills/` (managed skills)\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent.md:64:- Managed/local: `~/.openclaw/skills`\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/multi-agent.md:40:Skills are loaded from each agent workspace plus shared roots such as `~/.openclaw/skills`, then filtered by the effective agent skill allowlist when configured. Use `agents.defaults.skills` for a shared baseline and `agents.list[].skills` for per-agent replacement. See [Skills: per-agent vs shared](/tools/skills#per-agent-vs-shared-skills) and [Skills: agent skill allowlists](/tools/skills#agent-skill-allowlists).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/cli/migrate.md:135:- Personal AgentSkills under `$HOME/.agents/skills`, copied into the current\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/application-modernization-plan.md:155:create `.agents/skills/openclaw-frontend/SKILL.md` first, keep the frontmatter\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/platforms/mac/skills.md:33:- The app stores keys in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` under `skills.entries.<skillKey>`.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/help/faq.md:171:    Use managed overrides instead of editing the repo copy. Put your changes in `~/.openclaw/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (or add a folder via `skills.load.extraDirs` in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`). Precedence is `<workspace>/skills` → `<workspace>/.agents/skills` → `~/.agents/skills` → `~/.openclaw/skills` → bundled → `skills.load.extraDirs`, so managed overrides still win over bundled skills without touching git. If you need the skill installed globally but only visible to some agents, keep the shared copy in `~/.openclaw/skills` and control visibility with `agents.defaults.skills` and `agents.list[].skills`. Only upstream-worthy edits should live in the repo and go out as PRs.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/help/faq.md:175:    Yes. Add extra directories via `skills.load.extraDirs` in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` (lowest precedence). Default precedence is `<workspace>/skills` → `<workspace>/.agents/skills` → `~/.agents/skills` → `~/.openclaw/skills` → bundled → `skills.load.extraDirs`. `clawhub` installs into `./skills` by default, which OpenClaw treats as `<workspace>/skills` on the next session. If the skill should only be visible to certain agents, pair that with `agents.defaults.skills` or `agents.list[].skills`.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/help/faq.md:335:    `~/.openclaw/skills` and use `agents.defaults.skills` or\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/help/faq.md:353:    Not directly. macOS skills are gated by `metadata.openclaw.os` plus required binaries, and skills only appear in the system prompt when they are eligible on the **Gateway host**. On Linux, `darwin`-only skills (like `apple-notes`, `apple-reminders`, `things-mac`) will not load unless you override the gating.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/help/faq.md:375:    3. Override the skill metadata (workspace or `~/.openclaw/skills`) to allow Linux:\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/help/faq.md:412:    Native installs land in the active workspace `skills/` directory. For shared skills across agents, place them in `~/.openclaw/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. If only some agents should see a shared install, configure `agents.defaults.skills` or `agents.list[].skills`. Some skills expect binaries installed via Homebrew; on Linux that means Linuxbrew (see the Homebrew Linux FAQ entry above). See [Skills](/tools/skills), [Skills config](/tools/skills-config), and [ClawHub](/tools/clawhub).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/help/faq.md:588:      and shared skills (`~/.openclaw/skills`).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/gh-issues/SKILL.md:134:  > \"GitHub authentication failed. Please check your apiKey in the OpenClaw dashboard or in the active OpenClaw config path (`$OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH`, default `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`) under `skills.entries.gh-issues`.\"\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/gh-issues/SKILL.md:232:   > \"GitHub authentication failed. Please check your apiKey in the OpenClaw dashboard or in the active OpenClaw config path (`$OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH`, default `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`) under `skills.entries.gh-issues`.\"\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md:3:description: Create, edit, improve, tidy, review, audit, or restructure AgentSkills and SKILL.md files.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/taskflow/SKILL.md:149:- See `skills/taskflow-inbox-triage/SKILL.md` for a concrete routing pattern"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":217,"aggregated":"/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/audit-checks.md:99:| `skills.workspace.symlink_escape`                             | warn          | Workspace `skills/**/SKILL.md` resolves outside workspace root (symlink-chain drift) | workspace `skills/**` filesystem state                                                               | no       |\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-examples.md:480:      { id: \"docs\", workspace: \"~/.openclaw/workspace-docs\", skills: [\"docs-search\"] },\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/plugins/voice-call.md:712:This repo ships a matching skill doc at `skills/voice-call/SKILL.md`.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/plugins/skill-workshop.md:21:<workspace>/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/setup.md:35:- **Workspace:** `~/.openclaw/workspace` (skills, prompts, memories; make it a private git repo)\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/install/docker-vm-runtime.md:129:| Skill configs       | `/home/node/.openclaw/skills/`                         | Host volume mount      | Skill-level state                                             |\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/clawhub.md:133:If you already use `~/.openclaw/skills` or bundled skills, workspace\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/clawhub.md:437:    `~/openclaw/skills` and `~/.openclaw/skills`). This is designed to\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/creating-skills.md:21:    mkdir -p ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/hello-world\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/creating-skills.md:111:| `~/.openclaw/skills/`           | Medium     | Shared (all agents)   |\n/usr/lib/node_mod