{"type":"message","id":"f8ddcc45","parentId":"b057bae1","timestamp":"2026-05-11T08:05:47.645Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_jgVf37C1oDLJQbZe9nu94NAW|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a018ddb2c988191adc94a4e1f042e6f","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/config-channels.md:39:`channels.defaults.groupPolicy` sets the default when a provider's `groupPolicy` is unset.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/config-channels.md:75:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\", // open | allowlist | disabled\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/config-channels.md:87:- `channels.defaults.groupPolicy`: fallback group policy when a provider-level `groupPolicy` is unset.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/config-channels.md:126:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/config-channels.md:378:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration.md:171:    For groups, use `groupPolicy` + `groupAllowFrom` or channel-specific allowlists.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:197:- **Trigger authorization**: who can trigger the agent (`dmPolicy`, `groupPolicy`, allowlists, mention gates).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:575:    - `groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"` + `groupAllowFrom`: restrict who can trigger the bot _inside_ a group session (WhatsApp/Telegram/Signal/iMessage/Microsoft Teams).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:577:  - Group checks run in this order: `groupPolicy`/group allowlists first, mention/reply activation second.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:579:  - **Security note:** treat `dmPolicy=\"open\"` and `groupPolicy=\"open\"` as last-resort settings. They should be barely used; prefer pairing + allowlists unless you fully trust every member of the room.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/audit-checks.md:110:| `security.exposure.open_channels_with_exec`                   | warn/critical | Shared/public rooms can reach exec-enabled agents                                    | `channels.*.dmPolicy`, `channels.*.groupPolicy`, `tools.exec.*`, `agents.list[].tools.exec.*`        | no       |\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/audit-checks.md:111:| `security.exposure.open_groups_with_elevated`                 | critical      | Open groups + elevated tools create high-impact prompt-injection paths               | `channels.*.groupPolicy`, `tools.elevated.*`                                                         | no       |\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/audit-checks.md:112:| `security.exposure.open_groups_with_runtime_or_fs`            | critical/warn | Open groups can reach command/file tools without sandbox/workspace guards            | `channels.*.groupPolicy`, `tools.profile/deny`, `tools.fs.workspaceOnly`, `agents.*.sandbox.mode`    | no       |\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-examples.md:185:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-examples.md:194:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/install/fly.md:185:          \"groupPolicy\": \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/install/exe-dev.md:147:      groupPolicy: \"open\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/install/exe-dev.md:155:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/access-groups.md:92:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/irc.md:44:- `channels.irc.groupPolicy` defaults to `\"allowlist\"`.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/irc.md:45:- With `groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"`, set `channels.irc.groups` to define allowed channels.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/irc.md:52:1. **Channel access** (`groupPolicy` + `groups`): whether the bot accepts messages from a channel at all.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/irc.md:60:- `channels.irc.groupPolicy=\"open\"` allows unconfigured channels (**still mention-gated by default**)\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/irc.md:82:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/irc.md:93:Even if a channel is allowed (via `groupPolicy` + `groups`) and the sender is allowed, OpenClaw defaults to **mention-gating** in group contexts.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/irc.md:103:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/irc.md:121:      groupPolicy: \"open\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/feishu.md:60:**Group policy** (`channels.feishu.groupPolicy`):\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/feishu.md:87:      groupPolicy: \"open\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/feishu.md:99:      groupPolicy: \"open\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/feishu.md:112:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/feishu.md:120:In `allowlist` mode, you can also admit a group by adding an explicit `groups.<chat_id>` entry. Explicit entries do not override `groupPolicy: \"disabled\"`. Wildcard defaults under `groups.*` configure matching groups, but they do not admit groups by themselves.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/feishu.md:126:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/feishu.md:143:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/feishu.md:204:3. Verify `groupPolicy` is not `\"disabled\"`\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/feishu.md:423:| `channels.feishu.groupPolicy`                     | Group policy                                                                     | `allowlist`      |\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:184:    - `channels.bluebubbles.groupPolicy = open | allowlist | disabled` (default: `allowlist`).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:223:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/bluebubbles.md:556:    - `channels.bluebubbles.groupPolicy`: `open | allowlist | disabled` (default: `allowlist`).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/group-messages.md:17:- Group policy: `channels.whatsapp.groupPolicy` controls whether group messages are accepted (`open|disabled|allowlist`). `allowlist` uses `channels.whatsapp.groupAllowFrom` (fallback: explicit `channels.whatsapp.allowFrom`). Default is `allowlist` (blocked until you add senders).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/group-messages.md:68:2. Say `@openclaw …` (or include the number). Only allowlisted senders can trigger it unless you set `groupPolicy: \"open\"`.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/whatsapp.md:62:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/whatsapp.md:248:    2. **Group sender policy** (`channels.whatsapp.groupPolicy` + `groupAllowFrom`)\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/whatsapp.md:258:    Note: if no `channels.whatsapp` block exists at all, runtime group-policy fallback is `allowlist` (with a warning log), even if `channels.defaults.groupPolicy` is set.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/whatsapp.md:275:    - with `groupPolicy: \"allowlist\"`, non-allowlisted senders are still blocked even if they reply to an allowlisted user's message\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/whatsapp.md:612:    - `groupPolicy`\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/whatsapp.md:616:    - duplicate keys in `openclaw.json` (JSON5): later entries override earlier ones, so keep a single `groupPolicy` per scope\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/whatsapp.md:653:- Group admission and sender authorization are separate checks. `groups[\"*\"]` widens the set of groups that can reach group handling, but it does not by itself authorize every sender in those groups. Sender access is still controlled separately by `channels.whatsapp.groupPolicy` and `channels.whatsapp.groupAllowFrom`.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/whatsapp.md:704:- access: `dmPolicy`, `allowFrom`, `groupPolicy`, `groupAllowFrom`, `groups`\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:123:Group chats are blocked by default (`channels.msteams.groupPolicy: \"allowlist\"`). To allow group replies, set `channels.msteams.groupAllowFrom`, or use `groupPolicy: \"open\"` to allow any member (mention-gated).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:155:- Default: `channels.msteams.groupPolicy = \"allowlist\"` (blocked unless you add `groupAllowFrom`). Use `channels.defaults.groupPolicy` to override the default when unset.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:157:- Set `groupPolicy: \"open\"` to allow any member (still mention‑gated by default).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:158:- To allow **no channels**, set `channels.msteams.groupPolicy: \"disabled\"`.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:166:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:177:- When `groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"` and a teams allowlist is present, only listed teams/channels are accepted (mention‑gated).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/msteams.md:188:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/line.md:139:- `channels.line.groupPolicy`: `allowlist | open | disabled`\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/line.md:142:- Runtime note: if `channels.line` is completely missing, runtime falls back to `groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"` for group checks (even if `channels.defaults.groupPolicy` is set).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/mattermost.md:195:- Default: `channels.mattermost.groupPolicy = \"allowlist\"` (mention-gated).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/mattermost.md:199:- Open channels: `channels.mattermost.groupPolicy=\"open\"` (mention-gated).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/mattermost.md:200:- Runtime note: if `channels.mattermost` is completely missing, runtime falls back to `groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"` for group checks (even if `channels.defaults.groupPolicy` is set).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/mattermost.md:208:      groupPolicy: \"open\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/telegram.md:65:    Add the bot to your group, then set `channels.telegram.groups` and `groupPolicy` to match your access model.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/telegram.md:153:         - with `groupPolicy: \"open\"`: any group can pass group-ID checks\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/telegram.md:154:         - with `groupPolicy: \"allowlist\"` (default): groups are blocked until you add `groups` entries (or `\"*\"`)\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/telegram.md:157:    2. **Which senders are allowed in groups** (`channels.telegram.groupPolicy`)\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/telegram.md:170:    Runtime note: if `channels.telegram` is completely missing, runtime defaults to fail-closed `groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"` unless `channels.defaults.groupPolicy` is explicitly set.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/telegram.md:180:          groupPolicy: \"open\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/telegram.md:559:    Topic inheritance: topic entries inherit group settings unless overridden (`requireMention`, `allowFrom`, `skills`, `systemPrompt`, `enabled`, `groupPolicy`).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/telegram.md:708:    - Reaction events still respect Telegram access controls (`dmPolicy`, `allowFrom`, `groupPolicy`, `groupAllowFrom`); unauthorized senders are dropped.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/telegram.md:987:- access control: `dmPolicy`, `allowFrom`, `groupPolicy`, `groupAllowFrom`, `groups`, `groups.*.topics.*`, top-level `bindings[]` (`type: \"acp\"`)\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/signal.md:196:- `channels.signal.groupPolicy = open | allowlist | disabled`.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/signal.md:201:- Runtime note: if `channels.signal` is completely missing, runtime falls back to `groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"` for group checks (even if `channels.defaults.groupPolicy` is set).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/signal.md:317:- `channels.signal.groupPolicy`: `open | allowlist | disabled` (default: allowlist).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/imessage.md:150:    `channels.imessage.groupPolicy` controls group handling:\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/imessage.md:159:    Runtime note: if `channels.imessage` is completely missing, runtime falls back to `groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"` and logs a warning (even if `channels.defaults.groupPolicy` is set).\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/imessage.md:292:    Each account can override fields such as `cliPath`, `dbPath`, `allowFrom`, `groupPolicy`, `mediaMaxMb`, history settings, and attachment root allowlists.\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/imessage.md:383:    - `channels.imessage.groupPolicy`\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/qqbot.md:149:      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/zalouser.md:95:- Default: `channels.zalouser.groupPolicy = \"open\"` (groups allowed). Use `channels.defaults.groupPolicy` to override the default when unset."}],"details":{"persistedDetailsTruncated":true,"originalDetailsBytesAtLeast":8193,"originalDetailKeys":["status","exitCode","durationMs","aggregated","cwd"],"status":"completed","cwd":"/openclaw/workspace","exitCode":0},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778486747644}}
{"type":"message","id":"7e98df71","parentId":"f8ddcc45","timestamp":"2026-05-11T08:05:49.695Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_oIVsOy7nEXjtxJ8AAIywnpME|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a018ddcd35c8191822109fcec2d2db3","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/channels/telegram.md","offset":145,"limit":45}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":3612,"output":38,"cacheRead":94208,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":97858,"cost":{"input":0.018060000000000003,"output":0.00114,"cacheRead":0.047104,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.066304}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778486747649,"responseId":"resp_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a018ddbcb548191ab3be35e7d209a5b"}}
{"type":"message","id":"21da3f78","parentId":"7e98df71","timestamp":"2026-05-11T08:05:49.700Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_oIVsOy7nEXjtxJ8AAIywnpME|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a018ddcd35c8191822109fcec2d2db3","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n  </Tab>\n\n  <Tab title=\"Group policy and allowlists\">\n    Two controls apply together:\n\n    1. **Which groups are allowed** (`channels.telegram.groups`)\n       - no `groups` config:\n         - with `groupPolicy: \"open\"`: any group can pass group-ID checks\n         - with `groupPolicy: \"allowlist\"` (default): groups are blocked until you add `groups` entries (or `\"*\"`)\n       - `groups` configured: acts as allowlist (explicit IDs or `\"*\"`)\n\n    2. **Which senders are allowed in groups** (`channels.telegram.groupPolicy`)\n       - `open`\n       - `allowlist` (default)\n       - `disabled`\n\n    `groupAllowFrom` is used for group sender filtering. If not set, Telegram falls back to `allowFrom`.\n    `groupAllowFrom` entries should be numeric Telegram user IDs (`telegram:` / `tg:` prefixes are normalized).\n    Do not put Telegram group or supergroup chat IDs in `groupAllowFrom`. Negative chat IDs belong under `channels.telegram.groups`.\n    Non-numeric entries are ignored for sender authorization.\n    Security boundary (`2026.2.25+`): group sender auth does **not** inherit DM pairing-store approvals.\n    Pairing stays DM-only. For groups, set `groupAllowFrom` or per-group/per-topic `allowFrom`.\n    If `groupAllowFrom` is unset, Telegram falls back to config `allowFrom`, not the pairing store.\n    Practical pattern for one-owner bots: set your user ID in `channels.telegram.allowFrom`, leave `groupAllowFrom` unset, and allow the target groups under `channels.telegram.groups`.\n    Runtime note: if `channels.telegram` is completely missing, runtime defaults to fail-closed `groupPolicy=\"allowlist\"` unless `channels.defaults.groupPolicy` is explicitly set.\n\n    Example: allow any member in one specific group:\n\n```json5\n{\n  channels: {\n    telegram: {\n      groups: {\n        \"-1001234567890\": {\n          groupPolicy: \"open\",\n          requireMention: false,\n        },\n      },\n    },\n  },\n}\n```\n\n    Example: allow only specific users inside one specific group:\n\n[840 more lines in file. Use offset=190 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778486749700}}
{"type":"message","id":"15996c98","parentId":"21da3f78","timestamp":"2026-05-11T08:05:59.633Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering group policy adjustments**\n\nI need to think about adding a group policy allowlist, similar to the default settings. Using a patch with this allowlist seems like a good idea. I wonder if this configuration change isn't expanding any risks? We have the explicit ORANGE setting for the browser, but adding the group policy might help maintain security as a default. It's important to mention this to ensure clarity!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a018ddfa1288191a535ca9600343d9f\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqAY3ko9bSy7XX-hVmXLaeNI_BmWSu6UBV_C4pjZ1eYnFjQwBavMDMUnzTReudhlz5g4OTh_h9tKM9rfXX_yQzwpLrtPWdWWW802avd7nCPVcqZFa3yhL8EPeHbT7lHF44T2tfjXhIp4OlDQWrcnb9QpivKXn_4CZ6MxDh-0du76lx_e2DVEmOFW_nfADinROUbC5RuOtBh_n4VXnTOTPo0YoPH6GGfe0nFMo-b33T8VWR1s7CnkKCf1nLBVp9ntXdKjQmMAwjxjuVG6RopO7xU85ew1LpY7D1hgXrULFqAzaGTy65feTqnAPGg3eFTPItI_fFt1cTS87fDrtNxSTnk01Cf3kZNPBZY4owVjaa5HBKpgZB5hEsm3X7734GI-SzbfW1y9sVpE1cmJ6m5Th0AEG83nILJBfHyXd0TI3lZ1697zHuDsuSaQNd5cB81chKdLUPeTdnNMKN_3vWF_AzulCdtxnuXotkXjBR0SX71C4nc_IlLjAinqeGmvYM5Yqv725kMc_sn6hDfc_msWx1XAvpxXPzN2VcldOet-QDRq8-PEhY0VlP4rAjiU-3J1cDZ7jxHPlAYdmzswcIu9Ra4pte1_97QN_JOFRkkOLvGMNi7FrOPVpUjuDqd6Mu73bYIV1r7QgAeU0H9czTdPrXNYl7XtEYsYaq-7tZy0Yg-0cZR9q0FKPR1BQSdVM-6AXF5PuBGJUUko6-nnkAMEzaANxY036AALWh_7OveCulQqDwOTi0lftawDEXYbjx677BOakpUTgGrZM0VQEWZ11O7C0bjXu3WlYeHVpjFPCgJJv6LgIWRvJg0z_v_mEU6-VWPqbI9BP9yNLmWe9uyDFkHtOCaAPa02FgAetuaGrNdq4i8ws7DHf-Qvzr_VcSyyMGt3Gt7HL_jBRAA75JkRVzXwElui3So_Ayd6Xn0XeOytnnabILTMoou9ZYJBSNe4bN_CFkU7kMxBjST3kLiGMHweqfkIalFHtZUYiHmBV3SvdcTbPfPSm61bbFaxERck1qES0DenSIqFB5SIji3T72NN12PTd5UcWFGQloRWCIvOoetE5oD-tHJrPgsRpcO45RI1inUnCBKT7mguLWynH0LyjqYlOatt7YEnWruGfx6tA07jpeJjfpK4LOU5J3kxpo1hV-ahVXzh-C6XM4KzuqE1LQIqX3e8QN1HjSDnj6YiRSOd2XrFunHVsFfVIcOOx1zAV3PVydnUdXBX-flqiyA6wZOw==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering group policy adjustments**\\n\\nI need to think about adding a group policy allowlist, similar to the default settings. Using a patch with this allowlist seems like a good idea. I wonder if this configuration change isn't expanding any risks? We have the explicit ORANGE setting for the browser, but adding the group policy might help maintain security as a default. It's important to mention this to ensure clarity!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"La herramienta oficial de config falla porque la configuración actual de Telegram no declara `groupPolicy`; aunque el gateway la acepta por defecto, el validador de parches lo exige. Voy a añadir `groupPolicy: \"allowlist\"` —que es el comportamiento seguro por defecto— junto con el permiso del browser, para que el parche sea validado.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a018de4818481918927d36932feb40f\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_VWISEipTLipzjBtsH0VHTlXY|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a018de4bd8c819192fe03f13d61be0e","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"set -e\ncat > /tmp/openclaw-browser-tool.patch.json5 <<'EOF'\n{\n  tools: {\n    profile: \"coding\",\n    alsoAllow: [\"browser\"],\n    web: {\n      search: {\n        enabled: false,\n        provider: \"duckduckgo\",\n      },\n      fetch: {\n        enabled: false,\n      },\n    },\n  },\n  browser: {\n    enabled: true,\n    defaultProfile: \"openclaw\",\n  },\n  channels: {\n    telegram: {\n      groupPolicy: \"allowlist\",\n    },\n  },\n}\nEOF\nopenclaw config patch --file /tmp/openclaw-browser-tool.patch.json5 --dry-run\nopenclaw config patch --file /tmp/openclaw-browser-tool.patch.json5\nopenclaw config validate\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- tools ---'\nopenclaw config get tools\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- browser ---'\nopenclaw config get browser\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- telegram groupPolicy ---'\nopenclaw config get channels.telegram.groupPolicy","workdir":"/openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":1062,"output":428,"cacheRead":97280,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":98770,"cost":{"input":0.0053100000000000005,"output":0.01284,"cacheRead":0.048639999999999996,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.06678999999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778486749704,"responseId":"resp_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a018dde04ec8191aabc7cacebb1e2eb"}}
