 may be movable and reorderable, possibly leading to content alignment issues. I think we can enhance the default using a CSS grid with dense auto-placement to minimize empty space. If the layout saved in localStorage retains the old order, it could create uneven gaps. Also, if cards don't fill the height, it can lead to more wasted space. The user mentioned images, so addressing that is crucial.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Modifying dashboard layout**\\n\\nI'm thinking about changing the layout to use `grid-auto-flow: dense`. If I set the breakpoints, maybe the system can use spans more efficiently. I should aim for compact cards that take up less space. Adding a \\\"dashboard rail\\\" sounds helpful but tricky. \\n\\nIf I adjust the current layout, existing elements could fill empty gaps better. So, I might make \\\"token-efficiency\\\" and \\\"tools\\\" span across the width, filling in those lower right corners. I wonder if updating the CSS will suffice without messing with user-localStorage? Let's edit the CSS instead!\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Analyzing layout issues**\\n\\nI'm noticing that using a \\\"section-kicker\\\" at full width might be causing unintended row breaks and empty spaces. It can force a new row that leaves gaps, especially under the system card. Maybe I should consider removing the Observabilidad technical kicker since it only slightly uses the full width. The alignment issue seems tied to how CSS grid adjusts rows based on the tallest card. \\n\\nTo optimize space, it might make sense to stack the system and smaller cards in a sidebar next to the BP.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Fixing CSS grid layout**\\n\\nI need to address an issue where the top row of a screenshot is full, but the lower part is empty due to CSS grid row height affected by a tall chart. A potential fix is separating the top hero into a nested two-column area, allowing the right rail to stack cards beside the chart. I’m considering simpler CSS using CSS Grid, like adding a wrapper section or setting a breakpoint to span rows, letting the side cards fill adjacent columns.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Analyzing grid placement**\\n\\nI’m considering how auto placement works after the system tries to fit the next available cell. For instance, if the blood pressure section occupies the first four columns across three rows and the system fills in columns five and six on row one, that’s promising. I’m thinking I need to set the grid rows for blood pressure to span three and perhaps make the system span two. But how do the row heights factor into this? If BP spans three rows, how does that affect the overall layout? I’ll explore the CSS grid specifications for further clarity.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Refining grid layout**\\n\\nI’m figuring out the grid layout: the system spans two rows in the first row. Compact cards will go in row two at column five while health fills column six. In the third row, habits will occupy column five and chaos column six, then security will take the first column and LLM the second in row four. I'm considering that a kicker will take the full width starting in row four. I might need to adjust placements to fill those spaces effectively. Setting the blood pressure section to span two rows seems ideal, maintaining balance throughout the layout.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"La captura confirma el problema: no es solo ancho. La gráfica principal crea una fila muy alta y el grid “espera” a que acabe esa fila, dejando huecos a la derecha. Voy a compactarlo con `grid-auto-flow: dense` y haciendo que la tarjeta de tensión arterial ocupe dos filas lógicas, para que las tarjetas pequeñas puedan rellenar el lateral.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a01913673148191810e600800e2fc54\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_LGyb7eYltBOrfpWOcWun7Vcr|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a01913723948191a1b354da1b68bdf9","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"set -e\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('/openclaw/workspace/dashboard/index.html')\ns=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('''      gap: 12px;\n      align-items: start;''','''      gap: 12px;\n      align-items: start;\n      grid-auto-flow: dense;''')\ns=s.replace('''    @media (min-width: 1850px) {\n      .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr)); }\n    }''','''    @media (min-width: 1850px) {\n      .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr)); }\n      #blood-pressure-section { grid-row: span 2; }\n    }''')\ns=s.replace('''      <section class=\"card span-2 technical\" data-card=\"token-efficiency\">''','''      <section class=\"card span-3 technical\" data-card=\"token-efficiency\">''')\ns=s.replace('''      <section class=\"card span-2 technical\" data-card=\"tools-plugins\">''','''      <section class=\"card span-3 technical\" data-card=\"tools-plugins\">''')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom html.parser import HTMLParser\nfrom pathlib import Path\nHTMLParser().feed(Path('/openclaw/workspace/dashboard/index.html').read_text())\nprint('html parse ok')\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY' >/tmp/dashboard-bp.js\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\ns=Path('/openclaw/workspace/dashboard/index.html').read_text()\nprint(re.findall(r'<script>(.*?)</script>', s, re.S)[0])\nPY\nnode --check /tmp/dashboard-bp.js\npython3 -m http.server 8766 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory /openclaw/workspace >/tmp/dashboard-test.log 2>&1 & pid=$!; sleep 1\ncurl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8766/dashboard/ | grep -q 'grid-auto-flow: dense'\nkill $pid; wait $pid 2>/dev/null || true\nprintf '%s\\n' '- Tras captura de Albert, se ajustó el grid para reducir huecos: `grid-auto-flow: dense`, tensión arterial ocupa 2 filas lógicas en pantallas grandes, y los bloques técnicos inferiores pasan a span-3 para llenar la fila completa.' >> /openclaw/workspace/memory/2026/05/11.md\necho 'dashboard dense grid check ok'","workdir":"/openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":1469,"output":2241,"cacheRead":107008,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":110718,"cost":{"input":0.007345000000000001,"output":0.06723,"cacheRead":0.053503999999999996,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.128079}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778487565123,"responseId":"resp_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a01910d70988191922b86a3c40ecba1"}}
