{"type":"custom_message","customType":"openclaw.runtime-context","content":"[media attached: /home/openclaw/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_5---cc855efe-bba6-4596-94ef-73753e9808fb.jpg (image/jpeg) | /home/openclaw/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_5---cc855efe-bba6-4596-94ef-73753e9808fb.jpg]\nTo send an image back, prefer the message tool (media/path/filePath). If you must inline, use MEDIA:https://example.com/image.jpg (spaces ok, quote if needed) or a safe relative path like MEDIA:./image.jpg. Absolute and ~ paths only work when they stay inside your allowed file-read boundary; host file:// URLs are blocked. Keep caption in the text body.\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"chat_id\": \"telegram:8785888003\",\n  \"message_id\": \"635\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"8785888003\",\n  \"sender\": \"OpenClaw Bunker\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Mon 2026-05-11 10:20 GMT+2\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"OpenClaw Bunker (8785888003)\",\n  \"id\": \"8785888003\",\n  \"name\": \"OpenClaw Bunker\"\n}\n```\n\n<media:image>","display":false,"details":{"source":"openclaw-runtime-context"},"id":"3dccde0a","parentId":"e41abdbd","timestamp":"2026-05-11T08:20:58.362Z"}
{"type":"message","id":"d97c509b","parentId":"3dccde0a","timestamp":"2026-05-11T08:21:29.194Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Evaluating image response options**\n\nI need to decide how to respond to an image. The user seems to implicitly ask for a screenshot. Since the image is attached and visible, I can analyze it directly. However, I should be cautious with using the image tool since it's meant for images not already provided. It seems that adjusting the dashboard layout might fall under the YELLOW scope the user confirmed, so I think I can proceed with modifying it. Let's inspect the current structure instead.\n\n**Analyzing screenshot layout options**\n\nI need to determine what the screenshot shows and whether to use the image tool. The prompt has an attached media image, which I can’t see as text, but typically, I could analyze it. I’m imagining a grid layout with large BP on the left and system health on the right, with empty space below. I may need to implement CSS masonry or revise the structure with a named grid layout for better use of space. I have to be mindful that the rest of the items might just shift down, leaving gaps.\n\n**Planning grid layout for cards**\n\nI need to set up the layout for compact cards under the system. To do this, I have to make sure the blood pressure section spans certain rows explicitly, while the system occupies column 5 and row 1. The compact cards will then sit in columns 5 and 6 for the subsequent rows. For the CSS grid, I’ll code the blood pressure section to span 4 columns and rows. I should ensure that compact cards fit nicely in the right-side columns, allowing for two per row.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a01916e3ae8819198d2052b06c66929\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqAZF9hJHYDkNDdNXZSvl_aHxEZPD609_Ie1I1FW0Mhjp3bU6BoYf42Z43N5pNemHr5R3UOS3oNBhxJRzU87jyAQPuzk9MZ-06Voh6q3qIB3Ixt1DEzXlvVFp_ce8V6I7QezpiuMcQRm8aiDiSOyzfyEpMoh9i2a