nshot. Since the image is attached and visible, I can analyze it directly. However, I should be cautious with using the image tool since it's meant for images not already provided. It seems that adjusting the dashboard layout might fall under the YELLOW scope the user confirmed, so I think I can proceed with modifying it. Let's inspect the current structure instead.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Analyzing screenshot layout options**\\n\\nI need to determine what the screenshot shows and whether to use the image tool. The prompt has an attached media image, which I can’t see as text, but typically, I could analyze it. I’m imagining a grid layout with large BP on the left and system health on the right, with empty space below. I may need to implement CSS masonry or revise the structure with a named grid layout for better use of space. I have to be mindful that the rest of the items might just shift down, leaving gaps.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning grid layout for cards**\\n\\nI need to set up the layout for compact cards under the system. To do this, I have to make sure the blood pressure section spans certain rows explicitly, while the system occupies column 5 and row 1. The compact cards will then sit in columns 5 and 6 for the subsequent rows. For the CSS grid, I’ll code the blood pressure section to span 4 columns and rows. I should ensure that compact cards fit nicely in the right-side columns, allowing for two per row.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"La captura confirma que el “dense” no ha sido suficiente: el navegador sigue reservando demasiada fila por la gráfica. Voy a pasar a un layout explícito de escritorio: tensión arterial fijada a la izquierda y columna derecha para tarjetas pequeñas/sistema.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a01917dcabc819182d4af35a7b58642\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_qTu2QddVmzTNdl5QtjCRpc1i|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a01917df73481918be7be0f41d5f708","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('/openclaw/workspace/dashboard/index.html')\ns=p.read_text()\n# Add desktop explicit placement overrides after 1850 media block content\nold='''    @media (min-width: 1850px) {\n      .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr)); }\n      #blood-pressure-section { grid-row: span 2; }\n    }'''\nnew='''    @media (min-width: 1850px) {\n      .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr)); }\n      #blood-pressure-section {\n        grid-column: 1 / span 4;\n        grid-row: 1 / span 5;\n      }\n      [data-card=\"system-health\"] { grid-column: 5 / span 2; grid-row: 1; }\n      [data-card=\"today\"] { grid-column: 5; grid-row: 2; }\n      [data-card=\"health-mobility\"] { grid-column: 6; grid-row: 2; }\n      [data-card=\"habits\"] { grid-column: 5; grid-row: 3; }\n      [data-card=\"chaos\"] { grid-column: 6; grid-row: 3; }\n      [data-card=\"security\"] { grid-column: 5; grid-row: 4; }\n      [data-card=\"llm-tokens\"] { grid-column: 6; grid-row: 4; }\n      .section-kicker { grid-row: 6; }\n      [data-card=\"token-efficiency\"] { grid-column: 1 / span 3; }\n      [data-card=\"tools-plugins\"] { grid-column: 4 / span 3; }\n    }'''\nif old not in s:\n    raise SystemExit('target block not found')\ns=s.replace(old,new)\n# Make BP chart less tall so table + side cards fit a 1080p viewport better\ns=s.replace('''      height: clamp(300px, 36vh, 420px);''','''      height: clamp(260px, 30vh, 340px);''')\n# Slightly reduce compact card minimum height\ns=s.replace('''    .compact { min-height: 104px; }''','''    .compact { min-height: 94px; }''')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom html.parser import HTMLParser\nfrom pathlib import Path\nHTMLParser().feed(Path('/openclaw/workspace/dashboard/index.html').read_text())\nprint('html parse ok')\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY' >/tmp/dashboard-bp.js\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\ns=Path('/openclaw/workspace/dashboard/index.html').read_text()\nprint(re.findall(r'<script>(.*?)</script>', s, re.S)[0])\nPY\nnode --check /tmp/dashboard-bp.js\npython3 -m http.server 8766 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory /openclaw/workspace >/tmp/dashboard-test.log 2>&1 & pid=$!; sleep 1\ncurl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8766/dashboard/ | grep -q 'grid-column: 5 / span 2'\nkill $pid; wait $pid 2>/dev/null || true\nprintf '%s\\n' '- Tras nueva captura, se cambió a layout explícito de escritorio para >=1850px: tensión arterial fija en columnas 1-4, sistema en columnas 5-6, tarjetas compactas colocadas manualmente en la derecha y técnicos abajo. Gráfica algo más baja para 1080p.' >> /openclaw/workspace/memory/2026/05/11.md\necho 'explicit desktop layout check ok'","workdir":"/openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":2918,"output":1477,"cacheRead":105984,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":110379,"cost":{"input":0.01459,"output":0.04431,"cacheRead":0.052992,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.11189199999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778487658362,"responseId":"resp_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a01916b2ba481918c3083e6091837bc"}}
