{"type":"custom_message","customType":"openclaw.runtime-context","content":"[media attached: /home/openclaw/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_6---650ae692-a6e4-4b9f-ae31-0c35f3336afb.jpg (image/jpeg) | /home/openclaw/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_6---650ae692-a6e4-4b9f-ae31-0c35f3336afb.jpg]\nTo send an image back, prefer the message tool (media/path/filePath). If you must inline, use MEDIA:https://example.com/image.jpg (spaces ok, quote if needed) or a safe relative path like MEDIA:./image.jpg. Absolute and ~ paths only work when they stay inside your allowed file-read boundary; host file:// URLs are blocked. Keep caption in the text body.\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"chat_id\": \"telegram:8785888003\",\n  \"message_id\": \"638\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"8785888003\",\n  \"sender\": \"OpenClaw Bunker\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Mon 2026-05-11 10:22 GMT+2\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"OpenClaw Bunker (8785888003)\",\n  \"id\": \"8785888003\",\n  \"name\": \"OpenClaw Bunker\"\n}\n```\n\n<media:image>","display":false,"details":{"source":"openclaw-runtime-context"},"id":"8ab625fe","parentId":"e006cfd1","timestamp":"2026-05-11T08:22:52.007Z"}
{"type":"message","id":"4ba79021","parentId":"8ab625fe","timestamp":"2026-05-11T08:22:58.229Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_QWRVmD5d0BFWMGI9An0Jj4Lt|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a0191e026e08191a521755048254f66","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/openclaw/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_6---650ae692-a6e4-4b9f-ae31-0c35f3336afb.jpg","prompt":"Analyze this latest dashboard screenshot. Focus on whether the layout now uses the full width, remaining empty spaces, and practical next CSS changes. Mention if content is cut off or if cards overlap."}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":2097,"output":97,"cacheRead":108032,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":110226,"cost":{"input":0.010485000000000001,"output":0.0029100000000000003,"cacheRead":0.054015999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.067411}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778487772007,"responseId":"resp_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a0191dcd6608191b5fd04f610185d91"}}
{"type":"message","id":"0df9eaae","parentId":"4ba79021","timestamp":"2026-05-11T08:23:27.482Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_QWRVmD5d0BFWMGI9An0Jj4Lt|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a0191e026e08191a521755048254f66","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The layout is **using more width than before**, but it still does **not fully take advantage of the available screen**.\n\nKey observations:\n\n- **Large empty space remains in the center/left-middle area.**\n  - The top-left chart/table area ends early vertically.\n  - The right-side cards occupy only a narrow column.\n  - The middle of the dashboard is mostly unused.\n\n- **Content appears clustered on the right side.**\n  - Several cards are stacked in a tight right column instead of spreading across the available width.\n\n- **No obvious card overlap is visible.**\n  - The cards appear separated correctly with borders/gaps.\n  - Nothing looks like it is sitting on top of another card.\n\n- **Some content may be cut off vertically near the bottom.**\n  - The bottom-left table is very close to the bottom edge.\n  - The page likely needs better vertical spacing or scrolling behavior.\n  - There is a visible scrollbar, so the dashboard may be taller than the viewport.\n\nPractical next CSS changes:\n\n```css\n.dashboard {\n  width: 100%;\n  max-width: none;\n  padding: 16px;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n}\n```\n\nUse a stronger grid layout:\n\n```css\n.dashboard-grid {\n  display: grid;\n  grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr;\n  gap: 16px;\n  width: 100%;\n}\n```\n\nFor the lower sections, make them span wider:\n\n```css\n.full-width-section {\n  grid-column: 1 / -1;\n}\n```\n\nAvoid fixed card widths:\n\n```css\n.card {\n  width: 100%;\n  min-width: 0;\n}\n```\n\nIf the right column is too narrow:\n\n```css\n.dashboard-grid {\n  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.7fr) minmax(320px, 1fr);\n}\n```\n\nAlso consider reducing vertical overflow:\n\n```css\nbody {\n  overflow-x: hidden;\n}\n\n.dashboard {\n  min-height: 100vh;\n}\n```\n\nOverall: **better than before, no obvious overlaps, but still too much unused central space. The next step should be restructuring the dashboard grid so cards and tables expand horizontally instead of staying clustered in narrow columns.**"}],"details":{"model":"openai-codex/gpt-5.5","image":"/home/openclaw/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_6---650ae692-a6e4-4b9f-ae31-0c35f3336afb.jpg","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778487807481}}
{"type":"message","id":"edcfb1d3","parentId":"0df9eaae","timestamp":"2026-05-11T08:23:55.279Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Evaluating layout options**\n\nI'm considering the layout for a graph. Using a full-width graph can eliminate empty space on the side. For a 1980x1080 setup, I could have a full-width page with a graph, table, and form while smaller cards are underneath. However, there’s a screenshot issue showing empty space—could be due to the drag-and-drop saved layout affecting the card order. It seems the grid is reserving too much area, creating that blank space, so I need to adjust the row settings.\n\n**Adjusting grid layout**\n\nI'm considering how to align the cards with the system. If I avoid spanning the BP (the big panel), the right-hand cards can line up under the system while leaving space for technical blocks on the left. This could reduce the empty center as well. I'm thinking of setting the BP to span four columns and two rows, with the system in row one and the cards in rows two to four. I also need to manage heights across the rows effectively.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a019205060c8191a7f943d9409fd69f\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqAZIVL-eXnw6fbEtLavtFFbosk7xCUsjZkDN80wl5jhboAJ6pb19eSqJoOM1P2CyfhshVPqWsbn3yCwQYVOSoOLTuwl2K8jk1XUpSrY-uKsIelhi5282Ju1_cYmjeZU-mDX0YC-bwNJyoAGEPueUxBkK1iCMK2tCBTVxlt6mRbSX4qnwcexc0TAvDYBQsiB7Hs4V5C-s-zc-2AX5GjYUyY8HGN_gqqcveIyoiTDnsrpHKN5JJJfeGj1ReHMdJlbpzHOngNLv879IHCmA4Q8LQXIpNCyPiGM6Kzo9JYcAX8_aPcixF6yW-xXIw8dy8iBGXKEMnddj7axMgsJBu9ClKqTEnAx7dBa4la42wLOb5AwnFAQSYFxAR3KmTdxPDltLh2ZUV7YbJDybGK_zM_YjXHEAC9KQ8RAE1Iu0M34jpZJg8Wqb_Bhn1Jq4suXpUOUU-XqsVKBoLc70vOCWVMeiFdEu8ZFWQ9lCOUinYn7MY9Hn5Kme4i0n_YzbvtKk2fH5IR7t5CEiS5g74Adc4XpjG7nDLkw0GtFBwdezVHZJM4QjWiBAN2L3EXSo88fa2OTSG2ZGsLRs0t-cNVO7Ylo05NijWwcYK3LeqWOqZ5NjEGShFvjozpBvYGm6jm6aqQKvYHzDPyjGL3bOCUdZSLGBd5hRaQY6YhM11JP5I3TElyWiDB1jS12lmo6x4OUk4y_lrXooIe3bWN5ZM4rCnVcL3dR