{"type":"message","id":"c31fdbe9","parentId":"8a526748","timestamp":"2026-05-11T08:33:59.816Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Revising dashboard structure**\n\nI'm planning to rewrite the HTML for the grid, but I'm concerned about nesting sections since it may cause validation issues. Instead, I'll use a `div` for class `dashboard-block`, which contains an `h2` for the title and child elements, possibly articles. The current CSS allows for nested sections, but I want four uniformly sized blocks. The mini cards within need to be draggable, so I might tweak the `initDraggableCards` function to only target the blocks. There’s also a potential bug with ellipsis representation that needs to be addressed.\n\n**Updating layout with Python**\n\nI'm thinking of using Python to replace the content from `<div class=\"grid\">` to the footer. I need to make sure to replace only the relevant CSS sections while preserving existing IDs. It looks like using cards as divs with specific classes could work well for this. My goal is to create four equal panels, which will make the layout clean and organized. I’ll have to ensure everything aligns properly once I make these changes.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a0194215f088191b5999d3094ac2383\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqAZQyVmox8W6XnV51RT5DK3zZNg6eL-1WoR5qqxzAyJJHEFR-ZegtkmqRKy2Gm42tSuGgeTq5mfvQmpHQF1mj0Is5Xv7xC84pfCzFRgzbpo6KkPQKB8BjsiYT67u6oJWGxmBczHKcz45vT33mb8I5gm8ZNi6gr8y_yNG8Sie3JY47ezZxxkshPQOKaFe15wdYf0HWixRJ17iFPL6OhKtl63y11DBiUFDuM0YvZJ-4F624uT7FhRj7nY2rKkFiIG_iSETaZk38mkdoR_wnzlZfNP-DRH0b0WkYCPmD7QxqOldELJn8GYwAF27_IA8cQ-lXyTwOsM-x3lgQ5Tvq1O9URaTq65flG3HC75jcphcSvNA9rIFBbhoeVEKgZKiHC_2m6aKcm9OE5M0BjBkzeUwYgp1L-_19kdZ1FJmV_eAsaL0ys88NDutDE7vxYrV5tyUYQaZldyNbuDepkR5ShVbbvLxfHQjgLM2lkGQAstJACBeMHOz7AH2Km5zvu-DqOs4yzBE-s7XDvnjOTcXkplFf8x7iSH2SjBCgYAP3935ZwsU9yHznigWLV73ddmUay5SIxCbPETAMtRrAC7r8sZLnpiCGDcnSamcwhGTsG-VpqhAT75BVRdl14Az2ONd