understand how to create the agent configuration. I'll refer to the documentation for guidance. It seems I've already read about the security skill, which is good. Now, I need to think about implementing the agent configuration. It might be helpful to look at the agents command help section for more details. This feels like a solid first step!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"Confirmación recibida. Lo haré por fases y sin darle herramientas de ejecución al validator: primero configuración/documentación local y validación; si OpenClaw soporta agente persistente con ese perfil, lo dejo registrado de forma mínima.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a019f358c488191b7cbb9b4aca2d8a1\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_HGEdabyvHMtDzE1tw06Thqpu|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a019f36074c81919b14eab8aa9fe185","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw agents --help 2>&1 | sed -n '1,260p'; echo '--- create?'; openclaw agents create --help 2>&1 | sed -n '1,240p' || true; echo '--- config schema agents snippets'; openclaw config schema 2>/dev/null | grep -n 'agents' | head -20","workdir":"/openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":30}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":1621,"output":207,"cacheRead":136192,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":138020,"cost":{"input":0.008105000000000001,"output":0.00621,"cacheRead":0.068096,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.08241100000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778491183087,"responseId":"resp_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a019f2ff7348191a77972b59a44118f"}}
{"type":"message","id":"7336e9d5","parentId":"f1d227b2","timestamp":"2026-05-11T09:19:56.977Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_HGEdabyvHMtDzE1tw06Thqpu|fc_08a4b4c6f9f74abf016a019f36074c81919b14eab8aa9fe185","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.5.7 (eeef486) — Claws out, commit in—let's ship something mildly responsible.\n\nUsage: openclaw agents [options] [command]\n\nManage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing)\n\nOptions:\n  -h, --help    Display help for command\n\nCommands:\n  add           Add a new isolated agent\n  bind          Add routing bindings for an agent\n  bindings      List routing bindings\n  delete        Delete an agent and prune workspace/state\n  list          List configured agents\n  set-identity  Update an agent identity (name/theme/emoji/avatar)\n  unbind        Remove routing bindings for an agent\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agents\n\n--- create?\n\n🦞 OpenClaw 2026.5.7 (eeef486) — Hot reload for config, cold sweat for deploys.\n\nUsage: openclaw agents [options] [command]\n\nManage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing)\n\nOptions:\n  -h, --help    Display help for command\n\nCommands:\n  add           Add a new isolated agent\n  bind          Add routing bindings for an agent\n  bindings      List routing bindings\n  delete        Delete an agent and prune workspace/state\n  list          List configured agents\n  set-identity  Update an agent identity (name/theme/emoji/avatar)\n  unbind        Remove routing bindings for an agent\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agents\n\n--- config schema agents snippets\n208:              \"description\": \"Enable log signal export through OpenTelemetry in addition to local logging sinks. Use this when centralized log correlation is required across services and agents.\"\n3370:          \"description\": \"Provider map keyed by provider ID containing connection/auth settings and concrete model definitions. Use stable provider keys so references from agents and tooling remain portable across environments.\"\n3419:    \"agents\": {\n3451:                  \"description\": \"Legacy input for agents.defaults.agentRuntime.id.\"\n3456:              \"description\": \"Legacy input for agents.defaults.agentRuntime. Run openclaw doctor --fix to rewrite it to agentRuntime.\"\n3702:              \"description\": \"Optional default skill allowlist inherited by agents that omit agents.list[].skills. Omit for unrestricted skills, set [] to give inheriting agents no skills, and remember explicit agents.list[].skills replaces this default instead of merging with it.\"\n3973:                  \"description\": \"Default max characters retained from AGENTS.md during post-compaction context refresh injection. Lower this to make compaction recovery cheaper, or raise it for agents that depend on longer startup guidance.\"\n4388:                      \"description\": \"Use this when you need directional transcript search across agents; add collections here to scope QMD recalls without creating a shared global transcript namespace.\"\n5595:                  \"description\": \"Maximum time in seconds allowed for a heartbeat agent turn before it is aborted. Leave unset to use agents.defaults.timeoutSeconds.\"\n5616:            \"subagents\": {\n5631:                  \"description\": \"Maximum nesting depth for sub-agent spawning. 1 = no nesting (default), 2 = sub-agents can spawn sub-sub-agents.\",\n6266:          \"description\": \"Shared default settings inherited by agents unless overridden per entry in agents.list. Use defaults to enforce consistent baseline behavior and reduce duplicated per-agent configuration.\"\n6310:                    \"description\": \"Legacy input for agents.list.*.agentRuntime.id.\"\n6315:                \"description\": \"Legacy input for agents.list.*.agentRuntime. Run openclaw doctor --fix to rewrite it to agentRuntime.\"\n6357:                \"description\": \"Optional per-agent default thinking level. Overrides agents.defaults.thinkingDefault for this agent when no per-message or session override is set.\"\n6395:                \"description\": \"Optional allowlist of skills for this agent. If omitted, the agent inherits agents.defaults.skills when set; otherwise skills stay unrestricted. Set [] for no skills. An explicit list fully replaces inherited defaults instead of merging with them.\"\n7324:                \"description\": \"Optional per-agent overrides for the focused context budget knobs. Omitted fields inherit agents.defaults.contextLimits.\"\n7376:                    \"description\": \"Per-agent override for heartbeat direct/DM delivery policy; use \\\"block\\\" for agents that should only send heartbeat alerts to non-DM destinations.\"\n7474:              \"subagents\": {\n7534:                \"description\": \"Optional per-agent embedded Pi overrides. Use this to opt specific agents into stricter GPT-5 execution behavior without changing the global default.\""}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":5579,"aggregated":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.5.7 (eeef486) — Claws out, commit in—let's ship something mildly responsible.\n\nUsage: openclaw agents [options] [command]\n\nManage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing)\n\nOptions:\n  -h, --help    Display help for command\n\nCommands:\n  add           Add a new isolated agent\n  bind          Add routing bindings for an agent\n  bindings      List routing bindings\n  delete        Delete an agent and prune workspace/state\n  list          List configured agents\n  set-identity  Update an agent identity (name/theme/emoji/avatar)\n  unbind        Remove routing bindings for an agent\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agents\n\n--- create?\n\n🦞 OpenClaw 2026.5.7 (eeef486) — Hot reload for config, cold sweat for deploys.\n\nUsage: openclaw agents [options] [command]\n\nManage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing)\n\nOptions:\n  -h, --help    Display help for command\n\nCommands:\n  add           Add a new isolated agent\n  bind          Add routing bindings for an agent\n  bindings      List routing bindings\n  delete        Delete an agent and prune workspace/state\n  list          List configured agents\n  set-identity  Update an agent identity (name/theme/emoji/avatar)\n  unbind        Remove routing bindings for an agent\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli/agents\n\n--- config schema agents snippets\n208:              \"description\": \"Enable log signal export through OpenTelemetry in addition to local logging sinks. Use this when centralized log correlation is required across services and agents.\"\n3370:          \"description\": \"Provider map keyed by provider ID containing connection/auth settings and concrete model definitions. Use stable provider keys so references from agents and tooling remain portable across environments.\"\n3419:    \"agents\": {\n3451:                  \"description\": \"Legacy input for agents.defaults.agentRuntime.id.\"\n3456:              \"description\": \"Legacy input for agents.defaults.agentRuntime. Run openclaw doctor --fix to rewrite it to agentRuntime.\"\n3702:              \"description\": \"Optional default skill allowlist inherited by agents that omit agents.list[].skills. Omit for unrestricted skills, set [] to give inheriting agents no skills, and remember explicit agents.list[].skills replaces this default instead of merging with it.\"\n3973:                  \"description\": \"Default max characters retained from AGENTS.md during post-compaction context refresh injection. Lower this to make compaction recovery cheaper, or raise it for agents that depend on longer startup guidance.\"\n4388:                      \"description\": \"Use this when you need directional transcript search across agents; add collections here to scope QMD recalls without creating a shared global transcript namespace.\"\n5595:                  \"description\": \"Maximum time in seconds allowed for a heartbeat agent turn before it is aborted. Leave unset to use agents.defaults.timeoutSeconds.\"\n5616:            \"subagents\": {\n5631:                  \"description\": \"Maximum nesting depth for sub-agent spawning. 1 = no nesting (default), 2 = sub-agents can spawn sub-sub-agents.\",\n6266:          \"description\": \"Shared default settings inherited by agents unless overridden per entry in agents.list. Use defaults to enforce consistent baseline behavior and reduce duplicated per-agent configuration.\"\n6310:                    \"description\": \"Legacy input for agents.list.*.agentRuntime.id.\"\n6315:                \"description\": \"Legacy input for agents.list.*.agentRuntime. Run openclaw doctor --fix to rewrite it to agentRuntime.\"\n6357:                \"description\": \"Optional per-agent default thinking level. Overrides agents.defaults.thinkingDefault for this agent when no per-message or session override is set.\"\n6395:                \"description\": \"Optional allowlist of skills for this agent. If omitted, the agent inherits agents.defaults.skills when set; otherwise skills stay unrestricted. Set [] for no skills. An explicit list fully replaces inherited defaults instead of merging with them.\"\n7324:                \"description\": \"Optional per-agent overrides for the focused context budget knobs. Omitted fields inherit agents.defaults.contextLimits.\"\n7376:                    \"description\": \"Per-agent override for heartbeat direct/DM delivery policy; use \\\"block\\\" for agents that should only send heartbeat alerts to non-DM destinations.\"\n7474:              \"subagents\": {\n7534:                \"description\": \"Optional per-agent embedded Pi overrides. Use this to opt specific agents into stricter GPT-5 execution behavior without changing the global default.\"","cwd":"/openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778491196976}}
